  "HDFS-15931": {
    "jira_id": "HDFS-15931",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Fix non-static inner classes for better memory management",
    "description": "If an inner class does not need to reference its enclosing instance, it can be static. This prevents a common cause of memory leaks and uses less memory per instance of the enclosing class.\r\nCame across DataNodeProperties as a non static inner class defined in MiniDFSCluster without holding any implicit reference to MiniDFSCluster. Taking this opportunity to find other non-static inner classes that are not holding implicit reference to their respective enclosing instances.",
